#### pub fn [patch\_style](#method.patch_style)<S>(self, style: S) -> [Text](../prelude/struct.Text.html "struct ratatui::prelude::Text")<'a>

where S: [Into](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/convert/trait.Into.html "trait core::convert::Into")<[Style](../prelude/struct.Style.html "struct ratatui::prelude::Style")\>,

Patches the style of this Text, adding modifiers from the given style.

This is useful for when you want to apply a style to a text that already has some styling. In contrast to [`Text::style`](../prelude/struct.Text.html#method.style "method ratatui::prelude::Text::style"), this method will not overwrite the existing style, but instead will add the given style’s modifiers to this text’s style.

`Text` also implements [`Styled`](../style/trait.Styled.html "trait ratatui::style::Styled") which means you can use the methods of the [`Stylize`](../prelude/trait.Stylize.html "trait ratatui::prelude::Stylize") trait.

`style` accepts any type that is convertible to [`Style`](../prelude/struct.Style.html "struct ratatui::prelude::Style") (e.g. [`Style`](../prelude/struct.Style.html "struct ratatui::prelude::Style"), [`Color`](../prelude/enum.Color.html "enum ratatui::prelude::Color"), or your own type that implements [`Into<Style>`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/convert/trait.Into.html "trait core::convert::Into")).

This is a fluent setter method which must be chained or used as it consumes self

##### [§](#examples-6)Examples

```
use ratatui_core::style::{Color, Modifier};
use ratatui_core::text::Text;

let raw_text = Text::styled("The first line\nThe second line", Modifier::ITALIC);
let styled_text = Text::styled(
    String::from("The first line\nThe second line"),
    (Color::Yellow, Modifier::ITALIC),
);
assert_ne!(raw_text, styled_text);

let raw_text = raw_text.patch_style(Color::Yellow);
assert_eq!(raw_text, styled_text);
```

